        "text": "You are implementing Task 13: Regression run and test report generator, for the Talium code-econ storage module — the final task.\n\n## Task Description\nRead your task brief: `/Users/sumandra/projects/talium/code-econ/.superpowers/sdd/task-13-brief.md` — it has the exact code for `utils/gen_test_report.py` and the test.\n\n## Environment\nCanonical interpreter: **`venv/bin/python`**. Run EVERYTHING with it (e.g. `venv/bin/python -m pytest ...`, `venv/bin/python utils/gen_test_report.py`).\n\n## What this builds\n- `utils/gen_test_report.py`: stdlib-only script that parses a pytest JUnit XML at `docs/superpowers/reports/storage-junit.xml` and writes a Markdown report to `docs/superpowers/reports/2026-07-20-storage-test-report.md` (honoring `STORAGE_JUNIT_XML`/`STORAGE_REPORT_MD` env overrides for the test).\n- `tests/server/storage/test_report_generator.py`: drives the generator via subprocess with env overrides and asserts the Markdown output (Total count, Skipped count, header).\n\n## Your Job (TDD, in order)\n1. Write `tests/server/storage/test_report_generator.py` first, show it fail (script missing).\n2. Implement `utils/gen_test_report.py` per the brief.\n3. Show the generator test pass: `venv/bin/python -m pytest tests/server/storage/test_report_generator.py -v`.\n4. GENERATE THE REAL REPORT over the full storage suite:\n   ```\n   mkdir -p docs/superpowers/reports\n   venv/bin/python -m pytest tests/server/storage/ --junitxml=docs/superpowers/reports/storage-junit.xml\n   venv/bin/python utils/gen_test_report.py\n   ```\n   Confirm `docs/superpowers/reports/2026-07-20-storage-test-report.md` exists and lists every storage test with pass/skip and a Total/Passed/Failed/Skipped summary line.\n5. Commit `utils/gen_test_report.py`, the test, AND the generated report + junit xml under `docs/superpowers/reports/` with message: `test(storage): regression test report generator and generated report`.\n\n## Constraints\n- Never write \"Claude\" / \"co-authored-by Claude\" anywhere.\n- stdlib only in gen_test_report.py (xml.etree, pathlib, os, sys).\n\n## Report\nWrite your full report to `/Users/sumandra/projects/talium/code-econ/.superpowers/sdd/task-13-report.md` (implementation, TDD RED/GREEN, the generated report's summary line, files changed, self-review, concerns). Then reply with ONLY: Status, commits (SHA + subject), one-line test summary, the exact path of the generated report, concerns, report file path. Work from `/Users/sumandra/projects/talium/code-econ`. Escalate rather than guess if blocked.",
